{"artifact_id":"Figure3","kind":"figure","asset_path":"figures/fig_2606.11182v1-Figure3-1-4a12ee28e16d.png","asset_sha256":"4a12ee28e16d3954c098ac79bb61c0f53f32e03426921350e7f06a386e39ff9b","source_pdf_sha256":"796f3e04db798f9440b33c43cddd15e562fe1980ae64dc6fae3921a25590f105","revision_vid":"0a909f74d2d249aeb21052eea43491be943c926d139499b2c26c8cdb181a3cf7","canonical_id":"2606.11182","section_vid":"c8ef81d1314a76d05ed6a7977a22a9e248b38a8923b70240fd1002a6e3886a21","detector_fingerprint":"pdffigures2-0.0.12-SNAPSHOT","detector_metadata_sha256":"ec1f5abbb08247424229907ee22e266dbc98411d1d20c017e69c71fd8194b9f2","page_index":4,"region":{"x1":56.64,"y1":86.88,"x2":526.56,"y2":228.96},"caption":"Figure 3: Three-stage training design and initialization selection rule. Left: initialization builds prompt set, exploration alternates router and prompt evolution, and convergence fixes the router for larger-budget prompt learning. Right: the greedy coverage rule for top-K prompts selection.","containing_section":{"relation":"containing","section_id":"sec-1~39","path_id":"1~39","title":"Figure 3 :","text":"3Figure 3: Three-stage training design and initialization selection rule. Left: initialization builds prompt set, exploration alternates router and prompt evolution, and convergence fixes the router for larger-budget prompt learning. Right: the greedy coverage rule for top-K prompts selection.","truncated":false,"section_ordinal":56},"neighboring_sections":[{"relation":"previous","section_id":"sec-1~38","path_id":"1~38","title":"Prompt evolve.","text":"After router evolution, R T+1 routes the full data into slot-specific groups: D T+1 tr,k = {(x, y) ∈ D tr : R T+1 (x; P T ) = k}, D T+1 val,k = {(x, y) ∈ D val : R T+1 (x; P T ) = k}. Each non-empty slot is evolved independently and in parallel. For slot k, Eevee initializes a temporary prompt pool B P,k and samples D PM ⊂ D T+1 tr,k . Prompt evolution also uses mutation and reflection, but without the router-specific analysis step: it proposes p mut from reference prompts and mini-batch examples, then directly reflects from question, target answer, model answer, and correctness to obtain p ref . The better mini-batch prompt p ⋆ = arg max p∈{p mut ,p ref } s mb (p) is evaluated on the routed validation set with score s k val (•).","truncated":false,"section_ordinal":55},{"relation":"next","section_id":"sec-1~40","path_id":"1~40","title":"Figure 4 :","text":"4Figure4: Single-benchmark results[15,22]. Bars show final scores after learning on each benchmark independently. The no-router variant keeps a single retained prompt and therefore isolates prompt learning without router specialization.","truncated":false,"section_ordinal":57}],"reference_excerpts":[{"section_id":"sec-1~11","path_id":"1~11","title":"Initialization.","matched_form":"figure 3","excerpt":"Router evolution needs a prompt set that can reveal whether a routing decision is useful; otherwise accuracy reflects prompt weakness rather than router quality. Eevee therefore first initializes a diverse prompt set before router learning. Initialization runs prompt learning on the mixed training set and keeps a Pareto-front pool: because frontier prompts cover complementary examples, selecting from this pool yields specialized prompts with distinguishable behavior. Let B be the initialization pool after dominated candidates are removed, and let F i be the reduced Pareto frontier for validation example i. With coverage C F (p) = {i : p ∈ F i } and S 0 = ∅, Eevee greedily retains prompts by the rule in Figure 3, where ∆ denotes additional coverage. The retained prompts form P 0 and provide specialized behaviors from which the initial router can be written.","truncated":false},{"section_id":"sec-1~39","path_id":"1~39","title":"Figure 3 :","matched_form":"figure 3","excerpt":"3Figure 3: Three-stage training design and initialization selection rule. Left: initialization builds prompt set, exploration alternates router and prompt evolution, and convergence fixes the router for larger-budget prompt learning. Right: the greedy coverage rule for top-K prompts selection.","truncated":false}],"article_summary":{"source_id":"grobid:2606.11182#abstract","source_text_sha256":"2c104c0238f167fdb99e9545da61ce0d1f09aaf3e6b7f2fbfa7e3f237f582b3c","text":"Website CodeIn this paper, we propose Eevee, the first multi-dataset test-time prompt learning framework for LLM agents, enabling test-time prompt learning under real-world task streams. Existing methods are largely designed for single-dataset settings, while real-world applications require models to handle heterogeneous input streams drawn from multiple datasets, domains, and task distributions, limiting their practical applicability. To mitigate cross-dataset interference, Eevee introduces a router that partitions incoming inputs into task clusters and assigns them to suitable prompt configurations. This design is optimized via a router-prompt co-evolution strategy, which employs interleaved router and prompt learning phases to address their mutual dependency. Experiments across multiple datasets demonstrate that the framework improves robustness under heterogeneous data streams while maintaining single-benchmark learning capability and efficiency. Specifically, Eevee improves average multi-benchmark scores by 10.38 and 24.32 points over Qwen3-4B-Instruct and DeepSeek-V3.2, surpassing SOTA methods GEPA and ACE by up to 37.2% and 48.2%.","truncated":false},"diagnostics":[],"total_context_chars":3879,"truncated":false}